{
  "id": "top-k-frequent-elements",
  "title": "Top K Frequent Elements",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "categories": ["heap", "hash-map"],
  "descriptionMd": "Given an integer array `nums` and an integer `k`, return the `k` values that occur **most often** in `nums`. You may return them in any order. The input is guaranteed to have a single correct answer — there is never a tie in frequency right at the cut-off.\n\n**Example 1**\n\n```\nnums = [4, 4, 4, 6, 6, 9], k = 2\n→ [4, 6]\n```\n4 appears three times and 6 twice; 9 only once.\n\n**Example 2**\n\n```\nnums = [7], k = 1\n→ [7]\n```\n\n**Follow-up:** can you beat `O(n log n)` time, where `n` is the length of `nums`?",
  "constraints": ["1 ≤ nums.length ≤ 10⁵", "-10⁴ ≤ nums[i] ≤ 10⁴", "1 ≤ k ≤ number of distinct values in nums", "The answer is unique"],
  "hints": ["Start by counting how often each value occurs.", "You don't need a full sort of the counts — a size-k heap, or buckets indexed by frequency, is enough."],
  "signature": {
    "functionName": "topKFrequent",
    "params": [{ "name": "nums", "type": "int[]" }, { "name": "k", "type": "int" }],
    "returns": "int[]"
  },
  "comparator": "unordered",
